// XP value per milestone tier, roughly scaled to how hard it is to earn (a 250-workout "Veteran" is
// worth far more than logging your first session). Missing ids fall back to a small flat value so a
// newly-added milestone never breaks this table.

// Level titles unlocked at each threshold — the highest one at or below the current level applies.

// Account-level XP/leveling. Distinct from the Strength Score (which measures how much you lift
// relative to bodyweight/population standards) — this measures ongoing ENGAGEMENT: showing up,
// building streaks, setting PRs, unlocking achievements. It never regresses and never caps, so a
// lifetime of training always has somewhere further to climb, unlike the 6-tier strength standards.
//
// XP = a small flat amount per workout logged (so the level keeps creeping up between achievement
